ame">Trajan's Dacian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 101–102 CE; 105–106 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">Trajan's Dacian Wars were two campaigns fought by the Roman emperor Trajan against the kingdom of Dacia, north of the Danube, in 101–102 CE and 105–106 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/trakai"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/trakai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Trakai</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Trakai is a town west of Vilnius in Lithuania, set among lakes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/trakai-voivodeship"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/trakai-voivodeship.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Trakai Voivodeship</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Trakai Voivodeship was a province of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania created by the Union of Horodło in 1413 from the former Duchy of Trakai.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tralee"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tralee.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tralee</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tralee is the county town of County Kerry in south-west Ireland, near the head of Tralee Bay.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/tran-cao"><span class="enc-name">Trần Cảo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Trần Cảo was the leader of a major revolt in northern Vietnam in 1516, provoked by the heavy labour demands and palace building of the Lê emperor Lê Tương Dực.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/tran-nghe-tong"><span class="enc-name">Trần Nghệ Tông</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Trần Nghệ Tông was emperor of Vietnam of the Tran dynasty from 1370 to 1372 and then ruled as retired emperor until his death.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tran-nhan-tong"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tran-nhan-tong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Trần Nhân Tông</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Trần Nhân Tông (1258–1308) was emperor of Đại Việt from 1278 to 1293.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tran-quoc-pagoda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tran-quoc-pagoda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tran Quoc Pagoda</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Tran Quoc Pagoda in Hanoi is regarded as the oldest Buddhist temple in the city.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/tran-quy-khoang"><span class="enc-name">Trần Quý Khoáng</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Trần Quý Khoáng, known by his reign name Trùng Quang, was the second and last emperor of the Later Trần dynasty, which resisted the Ming occupation of Vietnam.</span></a></li></ul>
